id=a52sxq_log_noise
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: less log and audit noise
author=kusti420
description=Deep dive 2026-10-16 (9.3.41): (1) SurfaceFlinger's QtiSurfaceFlingerExtension asks the A14 HWC to set a layer corner radius it does not support and logs "Failed to send SET_CORNER_RADIUS command to HWC" up to 39 times a second (5,844 lines in 8 minutes): log.tag.QtiSurfaceFlingerExtension=E (verified live: no more lines). (2) The kernel audits at most 5 SELinux denials a second, and harmless ones used the whole budget, so boot-time denials were lost (audit_lost 1138): the Samsung F2FS file ioctls 0xf514/0xf522/0xf528 (the 5.4 kernel has none of them; stock S26U allows them) and lookups of unset vendor display/GPP props are no longer audited. Checked against every neverallow of the built policy. (3) 9.3.43, while charging: services.jar BSOHChargingDataCollector logs every sample with an unconditional Log.d (~360 lines/min; stock S26U code, no debug switch: L.IS_DEV only gates the file log) and the A52s BT HAL logs every in-band-sleep UART wake at D/I (~170-350 lines/min; Bluetooth is "off" but BLE_ON for Nearby device scanning, ble_scan_always_enabled=1, stock): log.tag.BSOHChargingDataCollector, log.tag.vendor.qti.bluetooth@1.0-ibs_handler and ...-wake_lock = W.
